.TH "TAKO" "1" "Jun 2026" "Tako CLI" "Tako CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
tako-config-explain - Show inferred runtime defaults and config sources


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtako config explain [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the effective configuration that Tako will use after environment
expansion, environment inheritance (extends), default resolution, and
validation. When the selected environment extends another, the header shows
the extends chain and each environment-scoped value names the environment
that supplied it. This command does not contact servers or write files.

.PP
With --redaction, print only the redaction report: every config value Tako
masks in output and its marker label, each service's secrets, env and
envFile keys marked masked or visible with the reason, secrets that cannot
be resolved, the names kept public, and the heuristic pattern IDs. The
report never prints a value, never contacts servers and never runs secret
provider CLIs.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for explain

.PP
\fB--redaction\fP[=false]
	Report what Tako masks in output for the environment, and why (no values, offline)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default is ./tako.yaml or ./tako.json)

.PP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--env\fP=""
	environment to use (default: the only environment, else production, else the first alphabetically)

.PP
\fB--events\fP=""
	stream progress events to stdout: ndjson (human output moves to stderr)

.PP
\fB--host-key-mode\fP=""
	SSH host key verification mode: tofu, strict, ask (default: tofu)

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	output format: text or json (json reserves stdout for the final result document)

.PP
\fB--preview\fP=""
	preview environment to use (deploy, ps, logs, exec, history, rollback, config explain); -e then names its base

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtako-config(1)\fP
